Jonadab the Unsightly One wrote:
> Janis Papanagnou <janis_papanag...@hotmail.com> wrote:
>
>> Two of the best spells are IMO charm monster and
>> magic missile.
>
> When I was a tourist I used charm monster
> to get past minotaurs, but is it really useful
> often enough to exercise the skill?

I bet it rules on astral.  Pushing through crowds of pets has to beat
pushing through crowds of hostiles.

> Also, it's
> level three, so you'd really kind of need a
> lower-level spell in the same school to start.

Agreed.  Each school has a level 1 spell.  Practice with that spell for
the lowest price experience towards enhancing that school.  Use sleep
for the Enchantment school to build skill in charm monster.  I have done
a lot of jump spells while exploring new levels to enhance Escape school
as well.

>> One skill slot per XL available.
>
> Okay, but some things use up more than
> one, so it's not really that simple.

This is part of why you should only enhance any skill to expert if you
can explain exactly why it's worth that many levels given how many other
schools you could enhance otherwise.  Often dagger is the only school
that's worth going to expert in the early game.  Other than the
multifire missile classes, going to expert in any school is a trap to
get you to waste slots until you've covered the schools you will
eventually want.

At 6 slots unskilled to expert but 3 unskilled to skilled, it's better
to keep melee schools at skilled until the missile schools have been
maxed out.  I'll bring a samurai to expert in bow as sson as I have hit
skilled in long sword for example.

>> If you practice a lot you'll get marks in the
>> #enhance menu indicating whether you need more
>> XL to advance or whether you cannot advance it
>> (you'll see those only if you had collected
>> enough proficiency points to actually advance).
>
> Hmm...
>
> Must be either I don't know how to read it, or
> I've never got to the point where I'd practiced
> enough but didn't have skill slots.

That or you don't survive to the end of the early game much.  Which
would also explain why your idea of the early game is different from the
other regulars.  It takes a specific number of damage hits or sucessful
casts to be able to enhance a school.  This number does not change as
the game progresses.  The experience points it takes to gain the next XP
level grows geometrically.  Thus it ends up seeming that skill
enhancement offers are rare in the early game, standard in the mid-game
and on.

There are * and # for maxed out and can be enhanced.  You'll get "You
feel you could be more dangerous" if you enhance a skill and there are
more enhancements available.


